&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;| Slowloris DOS attack
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;| State: LIKELY VULNERABLE
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;| IDs: CVE:CVE-2007-6750
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;| Slowloris tries to keep many connections to the target web server open and hold
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;| them open as long as possible. It accomplishes this by opening connections to
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;| the target web server and sending a partial request. By doing so, it starves
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;| the http server&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;s resources causing Denial Of Service.
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;| 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;| Disclosure date: 2009-09-17
